    "title": "Boot or init script modified for persistence",
    "desc": "A program wrote to a boot/init script - /etc/rc.local, /etc/rc.common, /etc/rc.d, or an /etc/init.d service script. Commands placed in an rc or init script run at boot with the privileges of the init process, so appending a payload there is a durable persistence and privilege-vector foothold (MITRE T1037.004) that a package manager does not normally touch at runtime. The persistence rule covers crontab, systemd units and shell rc files; this covers the legacy rc/init boot scripts.",
